<section>
  <div class="heading centered">
    <h2 class="no-top-margin">FAQ</h2>
    <p class="paragraph m secondary">
      Common questions about Active Agent
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="accordion-container">
    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "How do I install Active Agent?",
      answer: "Add <code>gem 'activeagent'</code> to your Gemfile and run <code>bundle install</code>. Then run <code>rails generate active_agent:install</code> to set up the initial configuration.".html_safe %>

    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "What's free and what's paid?",
      answer: "The gem — the framework, every provider, and the self-hosted dashboard — is MIT licensed and free forever. The hosted platform (managed dashboard, team features, higher quotas) and the commercial gem extensions are paid. Services are custom." %>

    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "Which providers are supported?",
      answer: "OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, AWS Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Ollama, OpenRouter, Requesty, and RubyLLM (which unlocks 15+ more). Switch providers with one line of code." %>

    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "How does the hosted platform get my data?",
      answer: "Your app's gem posts trace JSON to our ingest endpoint, authenticated with your workspace API key — one YAML block in <code>config/active_agent.yml</code>. Self-hosters keep everything local; the wire format is documented and open.".html_safe %>

    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "What's the difference between the free gem and Pro?",
      answer: "The free gem covers the framework, all providers, and the self-hosted dashboard. ActiveAgent.PRO ($99/mo or $995/yr) adds versioned agents and prompts, pausable multi-agent workflows, cached reasoning traces, generative UI with human-in-the-loop controls, and email support." %>

    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "Do I need the platform to get observability?",
      answer: "No. Traces and metrics ship free in the gem's self-hosted dashboard (<code>rails g active_agent:dashboard:install</code>). The platform adds hosted ingestion, evaluations, conversation history, cost estimates, and team workspaces on top of the same pipeline.".html_safe %>

    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "Can I use Active Agent with existing Rails apps?",
      answer: "Yes! Active Agent is designed to integrate seamlessly with existing Rails applications. It works alongside your existing models, controllers, and services." %>

    <%= render "pages/components/faq_item",
      question: "Can I self-host everything?",
      answer: "Yes. The framework and the dashboard are MIT licensed with no limits — your agents, traces, and data never have to leave your infrastructure. The hosted platform and commercial gems are optional." %>
  </div>
</section>
